    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI've upgraded from nvim 11.5 and the lazy plugin manager to nvim v12 and the built-in package manager `vim.pack.add`.\n\nI've now noticed on running nvim and opening multiple files that my `vim.o.expandtab = true` is resetting on the second and subsequent buffers. It still set to true on the first buffer.\n\nIf I remove the mini.clue plugin and repeat this all buffers show `expandtab` as expected. I also get the issue when I remove all other plugins apart from mini.clue. So I have to assume mini.clue is causing the problem, but I've no idea why or if I'm doing something wrong.\n\nCan anyone see if they have the same issue and/or if you have any ideas on what I can try please?\n\n### Reproduction\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. My `options.lua` has `vim.o.expandtab = true`\n2. Run `nvim *.lua` to open multiple files.\n3. Running `:set expandtab?` on the first buffer shows `expandtab` as expected.\n4. Running this on the other buffers shows `noexpandtab`\n5. I get the same issue when running `nvim file1.lua file2.lua file3.lua`\n6. But not when opening a single file then opening another file via `:e file2.lua`\n7. This is using the basic `miniclue.setup({})` without any custom options.\n\nNVIM v0.12.0-dev-2058+g41068c77aa (the latest as of 18/01/2026)\n\n```\n    \"mini.clue\": {\n      \"rev\": \"e2f0c1eb3ce652e34b1e9a9c504a780acf3bd4e3\",\n      \"src\": \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.clue\"\n    },\n```",
