            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can reproduce. The reason is probably because 'mini.clue' inside its `setup()` ensures triggers for every buffer where they are intended to be. This probably \"finalizes\" buffer-local options for those buffers, since `vim.o.expandtab = true` is set *after* setting up 'mini.clue'. Since `vim.o.expandtab = true` sets the \"global\" value of the option and doesn't affect options for already present buffers.\n\nI'll take a closer look. In the meantime, setting `vim.o.expandtab = true` (or other similar options) *before* `require('mini.clue').setup({ ... })` makes it work as expected.",
