            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`. The issue was indeed that `require('mini.clue').setup()` made not-yet-loaded buffers load, which \"finalized\" their buffer-local options (which were not yet set by the startup script). Arguably, it might be not the intended behavior of Neovim and/or Vim. But even if reported, I don't think this will change for backward compatibility reasons.",
