            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I think this has introduced a regression. mini-clue is no longer triggering on a markdown `.md` file but is on lua `.lua` and Python files `.py`. It worked fine for markdown prior to this change.\n\nWhen in a lua file `:map` shows the mini-clue keymaps. \nFirst two lines of `:map`\n\n```\nx  <Space>     *@<Lua 252: ~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.clue/lua/mini/clue.lua:1333>  \n              Query keys after \"<Space>\"\nn  <Space>     *@<Lua 262: ~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.clue/lua/mini/clue.lua:1333> \n              Query keys after \"<Space>\"\n```\n\nBut they don't show when in a markdown file. \nFirst two lines of `:map`\n\n```\nx  [[          *@:<C-U>exe \"normal! gv\"|call search('\\%(^#\\{1,5\\}\\s\\+\\S\\|^\\S.*\\n^[=-]\\+$\\)', \"bsW\")<CR>\n\nn  [[          *@<Lua 222: /opt/nvim-linux-x86_64-nightly/nvim-linux-x86_64/share/nvim/runtime/ftplugin/markdown.lua:8> \n                 Jump to previous section  \n```\n\nI reverted the plugin back to the previous revision and mini-clue now works for markdown files.\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n\n:lua vim.pack.del({'mini.clue'})\n\n# Change vim.pack.add to add the version\nvim.pack.add({\n    { src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.clue\", version = \"e2f0c1eb3ce652e34b1e9a9c504a780acf3bd4e3\" }\n})\n```\n\nI've narrowed the issue to having an LSP for that filetype. I already have LSPs for lua and Python but not for markdown. When I enable harper-ls for markdown mini-clue then works.\n\nIf I disable lua-ls then mini-clue no longer works for lua files.\n\nI enable LSPs in my `init.lua` file after the setup of mini-clue:\n\n```lua\nvim.lsp.enable({\n    'clangd',\n    'basedpyright',\n    'css-ls',\n    -- 'harper-ls',\n})\n```\n\nI tried the set up of mini-clue after I enable LSPs but it still doesn't work.\nI can work around this so it's not an issue for me.",
