            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I think this has introduced a regression. mini-clue is no longer triggering on a markdown `.md` file but is on lua `.lua` and Python files `.py`. It worked fine for markdown prior to this change.\n> ...\n> I've narrowed the issue to having an LSP for that filetype. I already have LSPs for lua and Python but not for markdown. When I enable harper-ls for markdown mini-clue then works.\n\nYeah, this has nothing to do with markdwon files per se, but the fact that there is an extra LSP server attaching. With Neovim started as `nvim -- file-a file-b` 'mini.clue' triggers now indeed are not set up in 'file-b'. This is because [neither of currently tracked events](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/c163117900c17d4abf30bc09452a261c8536060c/lua/mini/clue.lua#L1232-L1242) trigger when entering it later (`BufAdd` is triggered earlier on).\n\nMissed that since I rarely open Neovim like that. I'll take a look.",
