        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I've tried to install mini-clue from the backlog branch but I've no idea how to do this.\n> When I list the plugins using `vim.print(vim.pack.get()` it only shows the main and stable branches.\n\nIt is in the 'mini.nvim' plugin (this repo). I can reproduce that everything works as expected with the following setup:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({\n  { src = 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', version = 'backlog' },\n})\n\nrequire('mini.clue').setup({ triggers = { { mode = 'n', keys = '<Space>' } } })\nvim.o.expandtab = true\n```\n\nWas just curious if that branch also fixes things on your end (maybe I missed something).",
