        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "When using the minimal config I couldn't get `<Space>` to trigger the menu so I changed it to `<C-w>`.\n\n1. On opening multiple files `expandtab` is always true. This solves the original issue.\n2. It doesn't require an LSP running for that filetype to trigger mini-clue. This solves the second issue.\n3. I then installed the backlog version over my main config and both of the above still work. So triggering works both when an LSP is running and when it's not.\n\nFantastic !",
            "created_at": "2026-01-21T20:02:45Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2229#issuecomment-3780897639",
            "id": 3780897639,
